      "id": 1,
      "text": "Smithville was founded when Thomas Jefferson Gazley built the first house and store in 1827, serving settlers and nearby Lipan and Tonkawa Indians.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.smithville.tx.us/195/History-of-Smithville",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1887, local businessman Murray Burleson persuaded the Taylor, Bastrop, and Houston Railroad to build a terminus, turning Smithville into a rail hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.smithville.tx.us/195/History-of-Smithville",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Smithville’s Independence Park, dedicated in 2014, sits near the original Gazley house site and hosts community events and outdoor concerts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.smithville.tx.us/195/History-of-Smithville",
